== BACKLOG.md:265-280 at develop (the ks444 pair)
  - Why deferred: needs a way to distinguish caller-supplied from server-supplied values in the
    error path; a design question rather than a fix, and the concrete instance is now closed.
  - Discovered: 2026-08-07 during KS-564 (live end-to-end proof of Option A).

- [ ] Bare connector writes on `/share` + `/lifecycle-events` record no actor at all
  - Where: `Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/routes/documents.ts` (`/:id/share`,
    `/:id/lifecycle-events`) with `services/provenance.ts` — `handleOnBehalfOf` writes an
    `action_provenance` row ONLY when the caller supplied `onBehalfOf`.
  - Symptom: KS-564 folds a non-UUID connector principal to NULL in `shares.shared_by_id` /
    `document_lifecycle_events.actor_user_id` (it cannot go in a UUID column). When the connector
    ALSO omits `onBehalfOf`, no provenance row is written either, so the row has no actor anywhere —
    "who shared this" is unanswerable for bare connector shares. Verified live 2026-08-06: a bare
    connector share produced `shared_by_id = NULL` and no `action='share'` provenance row; the same
    call WITH `onBehalfOf` did produce one. Not a regression (pre-KS-564 the write 500'd outright),
    but the audit trail is thinner than the KS-480 §6 design implies. Fix is likely to record a
    connector-only provenance row (no `onBehalfOf` triplet) for every connector-authored action.
